1. Project Title
Auto Ticket Classification using Flow Designer
2. Update Set Creation
A local Update Set named Project Update Set is created in ServiceNow.
Name: Project Update Set
State: In progress
Application: Global
The Update Set is made the current set so that the project configurations can be captured.
3. Custom Table Creation
A custom table named Incident WorkFlow is created to store school IT helpdesk ticket information.
The table contains an auto-number field to uniquely identify each ticket.
4. Field Development
The following fields are created in the Incident WorkFlow table:
Number – Auto Number
Caller – Reference
Category – Choice
Subcategory – Choice
Short Description – String
Description – String
State – Choice
Assigned Group – Reference
Assigned To – Reference
5. Category and Subcategory Configuration
The following Category and Subcategory choices are configured:
Category
Subcategory
Network
Wi-Fi
Hardware
Projector
Access
Forgot Password
Performance
Slow Computer
The Subcategory field is configured as a dependent field based on the Category field.
6. Flow Designer Development
A Flow Designer flow named Auto Classify School IT Tickets is created.
The flow is triggered when a new record is created in the Incident WorkFlow table and the Category is empty.
7. Automatic Ticket Classification
The flow checks the ticket information and automatically classifies the ticket according to the identified issue.
Wi-Fi / Network → Network → Wi-Fi
Projector / Hardware → Hardware → Projector
Password / Login / Forgot Password → Access → Forgot Password
Slow / Hanging / Slow Computer → Performance → Slow Computer
8. Email Notification
After the ticket is classified, the flow sends an automated email notification to the Caller confirming that the request has been submitted.
9. Development Outcome
The project development successfully provides the required table, fields, dependent Category and Subcategory configuration, Flow Designer automation, and email notification for the school IT helpdesk ticket classification system.
